From 10b691d26a77c80a91d60e1c3cb611e43055e7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:04:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Grouped fat GEMM: cp.async multistage pipeline, skip empty
 M-blocks

A rows and trellis words stream global -> shared with cp.async through
5 stages of 32-wide K (4 for K >= 4) instead of a register-staged
64-wide prefetch; one barrier per stage, placed so the stage's last MMAs
issue before the next copy and dequant. M-blocks past an expert's last
row skip their loads and MMAs. Epilogue stages 32 rows per round in a
padded (bank-conflict-free) tile, preloads routing per row and drops
one barrier per round. Accumulation order unchanged: grouped output is
still bit-identical to the per-expert kernel.

GB10, live MiniMax-M3.1 TP2 shapes (125 experts, 33,173 rows):
gate|up K2 21.3 -> 17.7 ms, down K2 scatter 14.1 -> 13.1 ms,
gate|up K3 21.0 -> 17.6 ms, down K3 scatter 14.9 -> 13.3 ms.
bench_fat_grouped_shapes.py now runs those live shapes.
---
