index f2852d2..05b6d89 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -62,6 +62,16 @@
 
 ### Changed
 
+- Grouped fat-expert GEMM (`exl3_fat_gemm_grouped`): A rows and trellis words now stream
+  global -> shared with `cp.async` through a 5-stage pipeline (4 for K >= 4) of 32-wide K
+  stages instead of a register-staged 64-wide prefetch, with one barrier per stage placed so
+  the stage's last MMAs issue before the next copy and dequant; M-blocks past an expert's last
+  row skip their MMAs; the epilogue stages 32 rows per round in a bank-conflict-free padded
+  tile. Outputs are bit-identical to the per-expert kernel (same per-element K order). GB10,
+  live MiniMax-M3.1 TP2 shapes (125 experts, 33,173 rows): gate|up K2 21.3 -> 17.7 ms
+  (58.7 -> 70.6 TFLOPS), down K2 scatter 14.1 -> 13.1 ms, gate|up K3 21.0 -> 17.6 ms, down K3
+  14.9 -> 13.3 ms.
+
 - Unified `exl3_moe_mixedk` is the default mixed-K dispatch on every device.
   Per-K-group dispatch costs one launch plus ~9 ATen kernels per K tuple per
   layer per step at `MOE_SMS_PER_EXPERT` = 8 CTAs of 48, and at decode a group
